  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NIHR RIGHT1:Empowering people with Cutaneous Leishmaniasis-Intervention Programme to improve patient journey and reduce Stigma via community Education</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A UK and low- and middle-income country (LMIC) research partnership, Empowering people with Cutaneous Leishmaniasis: Intervention Programme to improve patient journey and reduce Stigma via community Education (ECLIPSE) is a five-year healthcare programme which aims to improve the cutaneous leishmaniasis (CL) patient journey and reduce stigma in the most marginalised and underserved communities in Brazil, Ethiopia and Sri Lanka.</narrative>
  </description>
